        "number": 12,
        "internalPageId": 12,
        "title": "Sentences Questions 0. I was calling him when the tornado took him away. Were you calling him when the tornado took him away? 1. She was eating lunch when the wave crashed the land. 2. They were watching the volcano while it was making eruption. 3. You were driving too fast when you crashed into his car. 4. It was raining a lot while the city was flooding. 5. We were having a good time when the fire started.",
        "visibleTexts": [
